! Store Zero to the INDICATOR register (Z,$IND) clears the settable
! indicator bits 20-63 (Reference Manual p.41: bits 0-19 are read-only).
! This is how the FP diagnostic resets the arithmetic indicators before
! a test (jb_af1c uses `Z,$IND` throughout, e.g. before every KR in
! routine F202G). It was a no-op until now (StretchStorage.writeWord(11)
! drops the write); the Store-Zero arm now folds the clear into `ind`,
! the same fix used for Branch on Bit changing an indicator bit
! (bb_indicator.strap / commit 63721f1).
!
!   L(U),CONST / K(U),CONST -> compare a value to itself: AE on, AH off
!   BB1,$AH,BAD             -> sets AH := 1 (AH was off, so no branch)
!   Z,$IND                  -> clears bits 20-63, so AH := 0
!   BB,$AH,FAIL             -> AH is off now, so NO branch (good)
!   B,PASS
! If Z,$IND fails to clear AH (the old no-op), the BB,$AH branches to
! FAIL. PC alone distinguishes: PASS (Z cleared it) vs FAIL (it did not).
!
! Injection (the indicator-clear fold removed, i.e. writeWord(11) drops
! the Z): halts at FAIL, as predicted.

        SLC, (8)2000.0
START   L(U), CONST
        K(U), CONST         ! AE on, AH off
        BB1, $AH, BAD       ! sets AH := 1
        Z, $IND             ! clears indicator bits 20-63: AH := 0
        BB, $AH, FAIL       ! AH off now: no branch
        B, PASS
FAIL    BEW, $              ! AH still set: Z,$IND did not clear it (bug)
BAD     BEW, $              ! BB1 wrongly branched on a 0 bit
PASS    BEW, $              ! AH cleared: success
CONST   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000125252525252525240

        END, START
